  "finalText": "I added the two bags to R1042 and charged Rosa $45.00 for them.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- R1042 now has 3 checked bags instead of 1. That's the most one booking can hold, so she can't add any more.\n- I charged one baggage fee of **$45.00** (4500 cents) to R1042. It's the only charge on that booking.\n\n**Why it's $45 and not $120:** Economy comes with 1 free bag and her Silver status adds 1 more, so 2 of her 3 bags are free. Only the third bag costs money, and the first bag over the allowance is $45. The $75 rate is for each bag after that, so it doesn't apply here.\n\n**Before changing anything,** I re-checked the booking (confirmed, economy, 1 bag, flight AS420 from San Francisco to Seattle on 2026-08-11, still scheduled), her Silver tier, the baggage rules, and that no fees had been charged on R1042 yet. Everything matched the plan. Today's date here (2026-10-06) is after the flight date, but the airline system's own date is 2026-07-28 and still shows the flight as scheduled, so I went by the system date. I didn't touch the fare, cabin, flight, her passenger record or any other booking.\n\n**Message for Rosa:** \"You now have 3 checked bags on R1042, which is the most one booking can hold. Economy includes one free bag and your Silver status adds another, so you only pay for the third bag: $45.00.\"",
